---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { property } from '../data/property';
const a = property.agent;
const updated = 'October 9, 2026';
---

<Base title={`Privacy notice | ${property.name}`} description="How this property website handles showing requests and visitor data." path="/privacy/" minimalChrome>
  <section class="section legal-page">
    <div class="container--narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notice</p>
      <h1 class="display display--lg">Your information, plainly.</h1>
      <p class="muted updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <div class="body-copy prose">
        <h2>Who runs this website</h2>
        <p>
          {property.address.streetDisplay} ({property.name}) is an independent marketing website for a single property.
          It is not the MLS and is not the website of {a.brokerage}. The property is listed by {a.name} ({a.license}),
          {a.title}, {a.brokerage}.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect when you request a showing</h2>
        <p>
          Your name and email address, your phone number if you choose to give it, the showing type (in person or live
          video) and any message you write, such as days or times that suit you. We also record how you found the site
          (campaign tags such as utm_source, ad click identifiers such as gclid or fbclid, the referring website and the
          landing page), the time of the request, and a one-way hash of your IP address used only to stop spam.
        </p>

        <h2>Lead forms on Facebook and Instagram</h2>
        <p>
          Some of our ads let you send your details without leaving Facebook or Instagram. When you submit such a form, Meta
          passes us what you entered (typically your name, email address and phone number, plus any answers to the form's
          questions) and which ad you saw. We handle it like a showing request from this website: it is stored with the other
          requests and sent to the listing agent, with a copy to the website's administrator. On its way to us it passes
          through a private Google Sheet in the website owner's Google account.
        </p>

        <h2>How it is used</h2>
        <p>
          Your request is sent to the listing agent so she can call you to arrange a showing, with a copy to the website's
          administrator, and you receive an acknowledgement by email. A showing is never confirmed by this website; only
          the listing agent can confirm a time with you. We do not sell your information. Apart from the scrambled contact
          details Meta may receive to measure our ads (see Advertising measurement below), it is not shared for anyone else's
          marketing.
        </p>

        <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
        <p>
          Requests are stored in a Cloudflare D1 database and emails are delivered by Resend. Requests are kept while the
          property is marketed and deleted within twelve months after it sells or is withdrawn.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          The site uses Google Analytics 4 to understand, in aggregate, how it is used: pages viewed, opening the gallery or
          film, clicks on showing or contact buttons, and whether a showing request was submitted. Google Analytics sets its
          own cookies and is governed by Google's privacy policy; you can opt out with Google's
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">browser add-on</a>. Your name, phone number,
          email, message and requested showing details are never sent to Google. Cloudflare Web Analytics, part of the
          hosting service, also measures page speed and aggregate visits without cookies.
        </p>

        <h2>Advertising measurement</h2>
        <p>
          The site uses the Meta Pixel to measure visits from our ads on Facebook and Instagram: the pages you view, a click
          to call the listing agent, and whether a showing request was submitted. Meta receives your IP address, browser
          and device details and the address of the page, and sets its own cookies (such as _fbp). When you fill in and
          send the showing request form, the pixel may also send your name, email address and phone number to Meta in
          hashed (scrambled) form, so Meta can match the visit to its accounts. Our server also tells Meta directly that a
          showing request was sent (Meta's Conversions API), with the same hashed name, email address and phone number,
          your IP address and browser details, and Meta's own cookie identifiers, so the result is measured even when the
          pixel is blocked. Your message is never sent to Meta. Meta handles this information under
          <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy" rel="noopener">Meta's Privacy Policy</a>, and you can manage how
          it is used for ads in your <a href="https://www.facebook.com/adpreferences" rel="noopener">ad preferences</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Bot protection</h2>
        <p>
          Cloudflare Turnstile and Cloudflare's automated bot detection check that requests come from a person; Cloudflare
          may set a short-lived security cookie for this. Turnstile does not require you to solve puzzles in most cases.
        </p>

        <h2>Map</h2>
        <p>
          The location map is an embedded Google Map. It loads from Google only when you reach it on the page; Google then
          receives your IP address and may set cookies, as described in
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          To ask what we hold about you or to have it deleted, email
          <a href="mailto:privacy@kalolipointparadisehawaii.com">privacy@kalolipointparadisehawaii.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="back"><a class="text-link" href="/">Back to the property</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-page { padding-top: calc(var(--header-h) + 4rem); }
  .display { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .updated { margin-top: 1rem; font-size: var(--step--1); }
  .prose { margin-top: 2.5rem; max-width: 68ch; }
  .prose h2 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 400; font-size: var(--step-2); color: var(--ink); margin-top: 2.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .prose a { color: var(--forest); }
  .back { margin-top: 3rem; }
</style>
